    {
      "severity": "questionable",
      "description": "The player has Emberheart Challenger on the stack (a 2/2 haste creature) and Stadium Headliner on the battlefield. With Dreadmaw's Ire in hand and the ability to attack, there could be meaningful combat damage this turn. The player chose not to activate any abilities during precombat main, which is likely fine since Fire Nation Palace's firebending ability is better used after declaring attackers (the mana is added on attack). However, the broader concern is whether the player plans to attack at all this turn - the sarcastic reasoning ('let's get to the part where I don't attack') suggests they may skip combat entirely, which would waste the haste on Emberheart Challenger and miss damage. Stadium Headliner with mobilize creates a token when attacking, and combined with Dreadmaw's Ire on an attacker, there's potential for significant damage. Not activating abilities precombat is reasonable, but the reasoning suggests a potential failure to attack which would be suboptimal.",
      "action_taken": "Declined to activate any abilities during precombat main phase while Emberheart Challenger is being cast.",
