    {
      "severity": "questionable",
      "description": "At 10 life facing a board with Surrak (4/3 trample), Badgermole Cub (2/2), Llanowar Elves (2/2 with Royal Role), and a land creature, Gem25P Snark is under serious pressure. Casting Leyline of Resonance for 4 mana is a value play that doubles targeted combat tricks, but it uses all available mana this turn, leaving no mana open for combat tricks like Full Bore or Dreadmaw's Ire that could help survive. The Leyline is powerful with the trick-heavy hand, but at 10 life against a board that threatens significant damage, spending the entire turn on a do-nothing enchantment is risky. An alternative line would be to hold up mana for Full Bore or Dreadmaw's Ire to potentially trade Stadium Headliner with Surrak on the opponent's attack, or use Fire Nation Palace's ability to give Stadium Headliner firebending for a big attack. However, if Snark survives, the Leyline doubles all future tricks which is very powerful with the hand of Dreadmaw's Ire and Full Bore.",
